ted and least useful tile. Keeping T3 pung, developing other pairs/sequences, and maintaining flexibility is optimal.\n\nReason:\nW3 is an isolated tile with very limited potential since W7, W8, and W9 are completely gone from unshown tiles. This makes it impossible to form a Pure Straight in Characters suit. Meanwhile, my T3 pung is strong, and I have multiple pairs with decent wait potential. Discarding W3 cleans up my hand and maintains flexibility for either a pair-based or meld-based winning strategy.\n\nAnswer: Play W3"}
